00.00000, 000.00000␀Receiver␀␀␀␀Found automatically: when the GPS does not answer at this speed, the device tries the others and keeps the one that works. This is where it starts.␀Serial speed␀␀␀␀The GPS rests between position checks and wakes on its own. It stays awake while the map, this page or Discover is open. The battery saver turns this on too.␀␀␀Save battery␀␀␀␀Check position every␀␀␀␀Privacy␀100 m␀␀␀250 m␀␀␀1 km␀␀␀␀Exact␀␀␀Others see your advertised position shifted by up to this much; your own map keeps the real fix.␀␀␀␀Location privacy␀␀␀␀30 sec␀␀Screen timeout␀␀Layout␀␀Huge␀␀␀␀Text size␀␀␀Portrait␀␀␀␀Portrait 180␀␀␀␀Landscape␀␀␀Landscape 180␀␀␀Orientation␀Bottom␀␀Top␀Left␀␀␀␀Right␀␀␀On the left or right it becomes a rail.␀Navigation bar␀␀Launcher layout␀Start over from a preset␀␀␀␀Off leaves the time to a clock widget when Home has one.␀␀␀␀Clock in the bar on Home␀␀␀␀Screensaver␀The mesh around you instead of a dark screen. Every ring is a real packet.␀␀On battery, show it for␀Always on when connected to power␀␀␀The mesh stays put instead of slowly turning around you.␀␀␀␀Keep north up␀␀␀Preview screensaver␀о‚є␀New messages␀␀␀␀A card with the message when one arrives while the screen is dark.␀␀At a glance␀Status bar & units␀␀Keeps your node's name off the status bar.␀␀Hide device name␀␀␀␀Distance in miles␀␀␀Temperature in Fahrenheit␀␀␀Minimal␀Moderate␀␀␀␀Strict␀␀Members log in with it to post. Up to 15 characters.␀␀␀␀Logs in as a guest. Blank lets anyone in as a guest. Up to 15 characters.␀␀␀0123456789.-␀␀␀␀Encrypted to␀␀␀␀Locked. Your pads and messages are encrypted with your passphrase. Messages that arrive while locked are kept and opened when you unlock.␀␀␀OTP Messenger␀␀␀Unlock␀␀Panic wipe␀␀%d B of pad left␀␀␀␀No chat contacts yet␀␀␀␀Add the other person as a contact first.␀␀␀␀Not available: everyone has its key␀Private channel␀No channels configured␀␀Add a private channel in Chats first.␀␀␀Use a private channel: Public uses a key everyone has, so a pad there protects nothing.␀Import pad file␀No SD card found␀␀␀␀Insert the card with the pad file and try again.␀␀␀␀/otp␀␀␀␀No pad files␀␀␀␀No .hex or .txt files in the SD card's top folder or /otp.␀␀оѓ—␀.hex files are imported as a new pad, replacing this one. .txt files are added as raw bytes.␀␀␀␀Settings␀␀␀␀Appearance␀␀The accent for the send button, the pad gauge and the status words␀␀Behaviour␀␀␀Play the message sound when an OTP message arrives␀␀Leave pad files on the SD card after importing them␀Keep imported files␀Passphrase lock␀On: pads, messages and the conversation list are encrypted on this device.␀␀Lock now␀␀␀␀Off. With a passphrase, everything is encrypted on this device and the app asks for it after every restart. Incoming messages wait until you unlock.␀␀␀␀Set passphrase␀␀Coming from the Lua app␀Moves its pads here with their counters, so you carry on in step with the other side. Afterwards remove the Lua app: two apps using one pad would burn the same bytes twice.␀␀␀␀Move pads from the Lua app␀␀20261012.native-1␀␀␀OTP Messenger %s В· wire-compatible with OTP_3_RC1 and MeshCore Open TAK␀␀␀␀Storage not ready yet␀␀␀Everything wiped. Protection is off.␀␀␀␀Wrong passphrase␀␀␀␀Too many conversations␀␀ (manual)␀␀␀%d B (max)␀␀%d B (QR-safe)␀␀Channel pad, shared by everyone on it␀␀␀One-time pad␀␀␀␀B left of %u␀␀␀␀Role %c%s  В·  sent %u B  В·  received %u B␀Offset %u  В·  shared by everyone on #%s␀␀␀␀Sync:␀␀␀not checked yet␀%d message(s) waiting for a path␀␀␀␀Open chat␀␀␀Check sync␀␀Add pad bytes␀␀␀Size to generate␀␀␀␀Generate %d random bytes␀␀␀␀Import a file from the SD card␀␀Paste hex␀␀␀о‚ћ␀Add text␀␀␀␀Share␀␀␀Show as QR code␀Check code␀␀Play the check code␀оЉѓ␀Listen for a check code␀Export to the SD card␀␀␀о…–␀Flip role␀␀␀Check code: the same on both devices means the same pad. Read it out, or play it by sound (Sound link) and listen on the other one; it reveals nothing about the pad.␀␀␀Show as QR code: MeshCore Open TAK scans it from its OTP Pad screen 