␀Asks for 4 numbers or letters to unlock, and locks whenever the screen goes off. If you forget it, the only way back in is to reset the device, which erases everything on it.␀␀Change PIN␀␀Export␀␀Export backup␀␀␀Off reuses meshcore-backup.json, the file name the MeshCore app uses.␀␀␀Append timestamp␀␀␀␀Saved to the SD card when one is in, otherwise to internal storage.␀Import backup␀␀␀From another firmware␀␀␀Replaces identity, channels and contacts with the backup's, then restarts. Import backup reads the MeshCore app's and Squatch Mesh's meshcore-backup.json, and MeshCore Open's contacts export (adds its contacts). From another firmware reads Squatch Mesh's /inw and MeshPunk's /meshpunk folders on the SD card.␀␀␀␀Saved backups␀␀␀No backups yet. Use Export backup above to create one.␀␀Factory reset␀␀␀Erases identity, contacts, channels, messages, Wi-Fi and all settings, then reboots.␀␀␀␀Tap a language; the device reboots to apply.␀␀␀␀What each installed app is allowed to do. Anything an app sends goes out under your node name and cannot be told apart from a message you typed. Private covers direct messages and room posts, and is kept separate from channels on purpose. Turn one off to take it back.␀␀␀␀No apps installed.␀␀Post to channels as me␀␀Read channel messages␀␀␀Send private messages as me␀Read private messages␀␀␀Send discovery probes␀␀␀Not asked yet␀␀␀Keep holding: settings␀␀Auto-refresh on␀Auto-refresh off␀␀␀␀Centered on %s␀␀Set your location first␀Reloading %d tilesвЂ¦␀␀␀Tiles cleared вЂ” reconnect Wi-Fi to re-download␀␀␀␀map_zfit␀␀␀␀No map levels found on the SD card␀␀Map file␀␀␀␀Folder tiles only␀␀␀пѓ ␀Team: pick the team channel in Team > Setup␀%s %s%s%s
